{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"constructors-new","title":"Constructor Functions & new","group":"Prototypes & Classes","order":31,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Before classes there were constructor functions. Knowing what <code>new</code> does step by step explains classes, <code>this</code>, and a favourite interview question.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-numbers\"></i>What <code>new Fn(args)</code> does</h3>\n<div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Create</div><div class=\"step-desc\">A brand-new empty object is created.</div></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Link</div><div class=\"step-desc\">Its <code>[[Prototype]]</code> is set to <code>Fn.prototype</code>.</div></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Bind and run</div><div class=\"step-desc\"><code>Fn</code> is called with <code>this</code> = the new object and the given arguments.</div></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">4</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Return</div><div class=\"step-desc\">If <code>Fn</code> returns an <strong>object</strong>, that object is the result; otherwise the new object is returned.</div></div></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function myNew(Ctor, ...args) {\n  const obj = Object.create(Ctor.prototype);   // steps 1 + 2\n  const result = Ctor.apply(obj, args);        // step 3\n  return result !== null &amp;&amp; typeof result === \"object\" ? result : obj;  // step 4\n}\n\nfunction User(name) { this.name = name; }\nUser.prototype.hi = function () { return `hi ${this.name}`; };\n\nconst u = myNew(User, \"Asha\");\nconsole.log(u, u.hi(), u instanceof User);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>User { name: 'Asha' } hi Asha true</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-back\"></i>Returning an object overrides <code>this</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function A() { this.x = 1; return { y: 2 }; }\nfunction B() { this.x = 1; return 42; }   // primitives are ignored\nconsole.log(new A(), new B());</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{ y: 2 } B { x: 1 }</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>Forgetting <code>new</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function Point(x) { this.x = x; }\ntry {\n  Point(5);                        // strict mode: this is undefined\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);\n}\nfunction SafePoint(x) {\n  if (!new.target) return new SafePoint(x);   // guard with new.target\n  this.x = x;\n}\nconsole.log(SafePoint(5));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Cannot set properties of undefined (setting 'x')\nSafePoint { x: 5 }</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-hierarchy-2\"></i>Inheritance the ES5 way</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function Animal(name) { this.name = name; }\nAnimal.prototype.speak = function () { return `${this.name} makes a sound`; };\n\nfunction Dog(name, breed) {\n  Animal.call(this, name);                         // \"super(name)\"\n  this.breed = breed;\n}\nDog.prototype = Object.create(Animal.prototype);  // link prototypes\nDog.prototype.constructor = Dog;                  // repair constructor\nDog.prototype.speak = function () {\n  return Animal.prototype.speak.call(this) + \" (woof)\";\n};\n\nconst d = new Dog(\"Rex\", \"lab\");\nconsole.log(d.speak(), d instanceof Animal, d.constructor.name);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Rex makes a sound (woof) true Dog</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>This is exactly what <code>class Dog extends Animal</code> does for you, with fewer ways to get it wrong.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What happens when you call a function with new?</summary><div><p>A new object is created, linked to <code>Fn.prototype</code>, <code>Fn</code> runs with <code>this</code> bound to it, and the new object is returned unless the function explicitly returns another object.</p></div></details></section>"}